  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the priorities identified by the governing bodies of the 2003 Convention, the activity aims at enhancing capacities for the safeguarding of intangible cultural heritage in the Caribbean SIDS.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In line with the priorities identified by the governing bodies of the 2003 Convention, the activity aims at enhancing capacities for the safeguarding of intangible cultural heritage in the Caribbean SIDS. The activity will pay due attention to the adequacy of institutional environments, frameworks for inventorying and the strengthening of national expertise in the field of safeguarding of the intangible cultural heritage.

The activity will assist the Caribbean State Parties to safeguard their intangible cultural heritage through enabling national capacity at all levels &#x2013; government, civil society, communities, academia, experts and practitioners. Capacity building activities are to be implemented in Guyana to advocate for ratification of the 2003 Convention. Capacities of Caribbean SIDS on the preparation of nomination files for the Lists of the 2003 Convention are to be strengthened. The activity will also support strengthening the capacities of key stakeholders in three pilot countries for the integration of living heritage into education practices and policies.</narrative>
  </description>
